WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.130
Oh, yeah...

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.280
We switch to summer uniforms today.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.600
Someone like Konata will probably
show up in her winter uniform.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.100
At least one person in our class will forget.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.850
Good morning, Sis.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.560
<i>There's one in this house.</i>

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.610
Rats!

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.480
I forgot to sign up for the TV drawing.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.190
Bah.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.740
I kinda wanted the prize.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.110
An apron from Apron of Love.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:04.030
Not enough love.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:07.620
You forgot because you don't have enough love.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:08.410
Not really.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:12.370
More like I've been busy with
student council stuff and tests.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:13.080
Nope, nope.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.040
Those are just excuses.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.090
I've never forgotten.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.050
Don't put me on the same level as
someone who only even thinks about having fun!

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:22.290
And the way you put it really pisses me off!

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.430
How do you win a drawing?

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:26.550
To put it simply...

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.970
Love!

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.100
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.430
I'm just a loveless woman.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.020
Well...

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.230
If you jot down the usual stuff...

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.020
...you're not going to win.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:37.650
What do you put on yours?

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.570
Stuff that'll help me win.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:40.740
How?

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.280
Good handwriting is a fundamental must.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.620
You have to design a postcard
that just begs to be drawn.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.620
Like what?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.240
Like...

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:53.330
Use a fluorescent marker to draw
a border around the postcard.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.800
That'll stand out.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:03:00.090
Then you add a picture related to the prize.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.670
A picture, huh?

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.590
I can't draw very well though.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.090
In that case...

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:09.610
...just send in as many entries as you can.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:11.930
I can probably handle that.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:12.890
But...

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:15.190
No matter how many you send...

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:19.860
...write each one out without using a printer.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.690
And send out a hundred each time.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.740
A hundred?!

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.780
Isn't that normal?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.530
Wouldn't that cost a lot?

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.950
You're fighting for something you want.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.370
That calls for passion and guts!

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.290
But wouldn't it be cheaper just to buy it then?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:37.460
Some things in this world can't be bought with money.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.380
Can you fit a hundred postcards in a mailbox?

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.880
You don't send them all at once...

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.680
...but a few here and a few there.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.430
And over the course of a few days.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:51.260
Depending on who's running the drawing...

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.770
...you might get caught.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:57.150
Well, sometimes you're
better off without the tricky stuff.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.900
And sometimes it's the exact opposite.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.360
So what do we do?

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.020
Like I said...

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:01.770
Love!

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:02.650
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.780
Anyway, if you want to win...

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.950
...glance through free newspapers and flyers...

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.990
...and look for drawings that
probably aren't going to attract many people.

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:14.080
You'll have a high chance of winning.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.750
I'll give it a try!

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.420
<i>Where's the love in that?</i>

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.500
You know, for twins...

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.100
...you don't look anything like each other.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.510
That's 'cause we're two-egg twins.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.100
So it's more like comparing sisters.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.890
One-egg twins look exactly the same...

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.140
...but two-egg twins can be...

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.100
...pretty different in appearance and personality.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:38.640
I see.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.810
Tsukasa is laid-back...

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:41.810
...but Kagami is pretty psycho.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:42.770
What was that?!

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.730
If you had the same hairstyles with the same ribbons...

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.570
...you might end up looking the same.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.240
<i>Kona-chan!</i>

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.320
No good.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.740
Kagami could never be the cutesy type.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:52.620
Zip it!

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.200
Don't insult me with your weird fantasies!

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.280
Can you use telepathy?

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:58.640
You know.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.620
With twins...

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.500
Even when they're raised separately...

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:06.380
...they end up having similar
lifestyles and significant others.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.590
And sometimes they end up
marrying another pair of twins.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.760
And when one of them is in danger...

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.720
...the other one can sense it
from a completely different place.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:17.270
There are all kinds of mysterious phenomena.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.350
So can't you use telepathy?

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.650
Give it a spin.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:21.190
Abracadabra!

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.310
You read way too much manga.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.770
Same with ManaKana...

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:26.070
ManaKana?

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:29.320
I heard that they have a few differences.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.820
By the way, Mana is the careful one...

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.530
...and Kana is the optimistic one.

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:37.080
And apparently they sound
a little different when they sing.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:37.870
That reminds me...

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:42.290
ManaKana thought they were
two-egg twins for a long time...

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:45.490
...but they recently learned that
they were actually one-egg twins.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:47.210
Seriously?!

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.840
Is it really that surprising?

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.220
The definitions for one-egg and two-egg twins...

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.090
...have changed recently.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.690
Which means that you two could be one-egg twins.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.330
Your identical traits would be...

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.480
You both like sweets, right?

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:03.950
Love 'em.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:04.610
I guess.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.360
You're both left-handed.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.110
That's right.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.320
What's your favorite color?

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:10.360
White maybe.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.150
Black.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.030
The same colors as your souls.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:14.430
What was that?!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.960
All this talk about eggs and black
and white cookies has made me hungry.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.040
Nobody was talking about food.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.130
It's suffocating in here.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.840
We just got on and I've already broken a sweat.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.930
It's that time of year.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.760
Hot...

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.240
They haven't turned on the air conditioning yet.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:46.980
H-Hey!

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:49.730
Hot...

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:53.070
Ladybug Samba, punk version.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:59.830
One of my cousins is getting married this month.

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.710
So she'll be a June bride.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:03.750
Sounds wonderful.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.170
How does this...

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:10.090
...wet and gloomy season
supposedly signify happiness?

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.300
Why does getting married in June make you happy?

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.510
The name June...

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.220
...is generally said to be...

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.850
...derived from the name of the Roman goddess, Juno.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:24.730
In Greek mythology...

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.150
...Juno is known as Hera...

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.400
...the goddess of marriage and fertility.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.650
Which is why those who get married
in Hera's month, the month of June...

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:36.450
...are said to receive her protection and blessing.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.990
But wasn't Hera Zeus's wife?

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.450
Yes, that's right.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.750
I have this image of Hera being extremely jealous...

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.250
...so I'm not feeling this happy thing.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:48.540
What?

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.090
Would you rather wear
a dress or a kimono for your wedding?

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.420
I would wear a dress.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.260
It's been my dream since I was a child.

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:00.220
I'd also go with a dress.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:02.430
But a kimono would also be nice...

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.780
I wanna wear both!

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:09.900
They have miniskirts and
really colorful dresses these days.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:12.570
A miniskirt wedding dress?

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:16.070
It'd look really cute with lots of frills on the hem.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:17.450
Lots of dreams!

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:18.780
Lots of frills!

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:19.950
Right?

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.950
You're Angel Salvia.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:22.540
Wait.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:25.280
Your hair makes you look more like Daisy.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:28.560
So a yellow top and miniskirt it is.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:30.920
Tsukasa-san.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.550
You'd probably look good in a miniskirt.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.550
Really?

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.710
Your dress is important...

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.340
...but the person you're getting
married to is also important.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:39.140
A childhood friend?

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:40.800
Or a rich lady?

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:42.890
Tough choice to make.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.890
One has lots of money...

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:48.340
...and the ability to cast Beho*mi and l***zun.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.100
But as far as feelings are concerned...

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.770
Bianca hands down!

00:08:51.770 --> 00:08:52.980
Oh, Kagami.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.480
You're the true love type, huh?

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.400
I thought you'd go for the money.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.440
No comeback, huh?

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.530
Yo, Konata.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:06.540
I've got a question about a
game I borrowed the other day.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.160
Oh.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.000
Hold it right there, Kagaminya.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.500
Isn't it more fun when you figure it out yourself?

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:14.460
You have a point.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:15.300
Yep, yep.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.590
Since you understand that
you should do things yourself...

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.800
...you'll do your own homework from now on, right?

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.350
Don't the detectives in manga and TV shows...

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:28.350
...run into an awful lot of murders?

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:30.440
Like in Conan or Kindaichi.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:33.400
There wouldn't be a story otherwise.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.190
Really?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.320
Couldn't they just solve normal cases?

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.320
Normal?

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:41.380
Like travel around Japan in search of missing persons.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.280
Tailing people would translate well into a game.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.450
With plenty of thrill and suspense.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:47.580
I guess.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.040
You could also conduct
investigations into unfaithful wives.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.880
Or look for pets that ran away?

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.340
Yep, yep!

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:57.070
But would that be fun to watch?

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:59.550
Probably no fun at all.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:00.340
Right?

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:01.380
Also...

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:02.840
Cases in real life...

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:05.760
...don't really use any brilliant tricks...

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:07.560
...like the ones you find in manga and TV shows.

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.020
I guess not.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:14.410
Fabricated fingerprints that can't be
detected through a luminol reaction.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.940
Stuff that's a step ahead of forensic labs.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:17.650
Well...

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.240
Anything too good might lead to copycats.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.240
Or be too sensitive for broadcast.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.700
Ah, or that...

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:27.870
The really hard cases end without
anyone realizing they happened or go...

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:28.540
...unsolved.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.960
That'd be wrong in so many ways!

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:34.830
Don't you hate how it's been
constantly raining the past few days?

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:36.540
You're right...

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:42.380
And I used to like rain...

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:43.930
You get soaked...

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:45.760
...and you can't hang clothes out to dry...

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:47.620
...so I've never really liked it.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.930
Why did you like rain, Kona-chan?

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:55.020
Because baseball games would be
canceled and I'd get to watch anime.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.230
I see.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.070
Sounds just like something you would say.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.990
They have a lot more dome stadiums now.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:06.910
Is something wrong?

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:13.120
You often see idiots and geniuses
going to the same school in anime...

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:14.750
Cease that immediately.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:15.800
Bite me!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.750
Get lost, neener-neener!

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.340
Isn't that actually kinda strange?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.460
If you put it that way...

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:22.880
...in some recent anime...

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:26.930
...the teacher looks the same age as the students.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.470
Or even younger.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.430
Teach.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.140
Yes, Ta*****na-san?

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:34.980
The world's always been interested in watching...

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:38.400
...the gap between physical age and mental age.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.190
Don't get it.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:42.030
You shouldn't question it.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.990
In fact, wouldn't a student who's
really different from everyone else...

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.030
...be the real mystery?

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:49.580
Yeah.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.990
I agree one hundred percent.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:53.950
I shouldn't be saying this...

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.540
...but I don't know how
you got into this school, Konata.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.600
You're good at putting stuff
off till the night before...

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.540
...so you didn't study
until the night before, right?

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:06.130
<i>What?</i>

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.470
<i>You mean she really did?</i>

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:08.140
Nah.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.960
Well, I couldn't have pulled it off in one night.

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.220
That gave me a scare.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:14.980
But I'm impressed that you actually kept studying.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:17.770
Did a quiz game come out for DS or something?

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:20.640
My dad set some conditions.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:21.980
A D-rank would mean a Pippin.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:23.610
A C-rank would mean a 3DO.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.650
A B-rank would mean a PS2.

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:26.650
<i>Papa Izumi.</i>

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:29.240
<i>You really know how to deal with your daughter, huh?</i>

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:30.780
I've been wondering...

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.120
Isn't the real mystery how
Tsukasa's in the same school as us?

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:41.590
She said it without even blinking!

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.710
Woo-hoo!

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:44.710
Come back in ten years!

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:44.920
I won again!

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:45.800
Curses!

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:45.840
I can't beat her at fighting games.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:46.630
I won again!

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:47.510
I can't beat her at fighting games.

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:48.930
She's spent way more time than I have.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.100
Challenge to me a different game if you want.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.350
Sure about that?

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.100
Then next is...

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.770
A quiz game!

00:12:58.350 --> 00:12:59.440
N-No way...

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:02.230
I lost to Konata in a game of knowledge?

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.190
Unbelievable...

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.190
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:06.490
<i>...she memorized the question order?</i>

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.640
Humiliated.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.530
<i>Her memory's incredible when it comes to gaming.</i>

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:12.200
What should we play next?

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.740
Don't be in such a hurry.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.080
Huh? That's weird.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.330
Didn't you have a really easy party game?

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:22.580
How do you know all the games I have?

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:25.550
You could probably beat me at that one.

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.030
It just stunk!

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:31.510
You've barely eaten any snacks, Kagami.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.510
Usually, you wolf them down.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:35.530
There's no real reason for it.

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:36.390
I know.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.640
Dieting for summer?

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.560
It's not like that.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:42.810
Not like you have anyone
to show your swimsuit off to.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:43.560
Shut it!

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.570
It's none of your business!

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:45.520
Oh, yeah.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.650
Weren't you guys born on Tanabata?

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:49.530
Isn't your birthday soon?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:50.570
What about it?

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:53.140
You remembered our birthday.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.120
Seventeen, huh?

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.290
Seventeen's right before the big one.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:59.040
What does that mean?

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.580
In the year before a critical year...

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.770
...unlucky things begin to happen.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:06.630
As our birthday approaches...

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.740
...I'm getting worried...

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.840
...so I bought a bunch of wards...

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.140
...and power stones.

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:15.010
That sounds like fun.

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:16.220
Sure is!

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:17.970
I couldn't stop buying them.

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:18.810
And like...

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:20.480
We have wards against rage at our place.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:21.230
Er, no.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:22.600
Wards against evil.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.240
Wards against rage, hah.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:25.610
Like...

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:29.490
We ensure safe pregnancy and protect
you from traffic accidents at the same time!

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:30.610
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.060
Oh, yeah.

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:35.680
Did you know that your birthday is Ponytail Day?

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:37.240
I had no idea.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.660
But why July 7th?

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:43.500
Because Vega from the Tanabata legend had a ponytail.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.500
Sounds like a stretch.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:48.960
There's a Japan Ponytail Society...

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:54.610
...and they give an award every year to a celebrity who they think would look good with a ponytail.

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.510
Really...

00:14:56.510 --> 00:15:00.020
But I have a feeling that anyone
would look good with a ponytail.

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:01.640
Sure about that?

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.690
My hair's the shortest...

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:10.730
...so it's barely a ponytail.

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:13.900
But a little ponytail's pretty cute.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:15.780
Yours also looks good, Kona-chan.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:18.370
You could go with that on an everyday basis.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.830
Think so?

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:21.690
Sure.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:28.540
S-Sis also...

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:29.590
Kagami's is...

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:30.340
Fine!

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:31.510
I get the idea!

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:33.300
I'll undo it!

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:34.800
All manly like a warrior.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.220
Sorry about that!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.390
Don't drunks often wear ties around their head?

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:43.310
Is that supposed to mean something?

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:44.270
Oh, that?

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.150
Isn't that just when the guy loosens the tie...

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:48.150
...and tries to pull it off over his head...

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:50.110
...but it gets stuck?

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:53.030
In that case...

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:56.570
...it's a lot weirder that
they're always carrying a takeout box.

00:15:56.570 --> 00:15:57.870
Takeout box?

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.280
The thing Kato-chan from the Drifters carries.

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.450
I'm not getting it...

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.120
Drunks these days...

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:09.290
...pretty much always have a tie around
their head and a takeout box in their hand.

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:10.340
Right?

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:14.300
I hope Vega and Altair meet this year.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:16.260
Shine. Shine. Shine.

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:19.050
Hope those rage wards of yours can deliver a miracle.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:20.390
Mind your own business.

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:24.900
They're giving away all varieties
of QUO cards at Comp Festival.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:25.870
Oh, yeah...

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:27.900
You're always collecting QUO cards...

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.350
...but do you ever use them?

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.220
I don't.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.230
Then why spend the effort?

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:35.610
Isn't it natural to want any item...

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.610
...related to a series you like?

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:39.530
As a fan. As a collector.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:40.570
Not really...

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:41.870
...if you're never gonna use them...

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.540
You can't use them!

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.250
You have to take good care of them!

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:49.370
It really pisses me off when I see someone use one.

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:51.790
You're not supposed to use these things!

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:55.630
Much less auction them off or sell them.

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.260
Using them makes you a surefire failure...

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:59.090
...as a fan and as a collector!

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:01.930
I really can't say anything when you're so worked up.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:05.600
In my case, I at least need three.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.600
One for preservation.

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:09.980
I keep it in a special case.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:13.150
Then one to take out occasionally to look at.

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:14.070
What's the last one for?

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:14.820
An extra.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:15.730
What's that?

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:21.500
Don't you always want two
or three of something you like?

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:24.410
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:25.240
You don't.

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:26.830
I'm just a geek.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:27.620
A weirdo.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:28.330
No.

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:31.630
I kind of understand what you're saying.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:34.670
You'd expect Tsukasa to be popular with guys...

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:36.630
...but I've never heard anything like that.

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:40.340
Tsukasa's a little plain and doesn't really stand out.

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.850
Isn't it because she's got a
scary sister guarding her like a hawk?

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.350
Did you say something?

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.520
I'm not sure if I'm really plain...

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:50.190
...or it's more that Kona-chan
and Yuki-chan are really unique.

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:53.440
Miyuki knows all kinds of things.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:54.230
And she's pretty.

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:55.360
Has a good figure.

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:56.570
Wears glasses.

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:57.610
Hates the dentist.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:58.110
Clumsy.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:17:58.530
Naturally clueless.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:17:59.240
Hey now.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:17:59.280
You kinda derailed there?
Naturally clueless.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:01.200
You kinda derailed there?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.450
But it's true that I haven't
heard anything about Miyuki.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:05.910
Maybe it's because she's so pretty...

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.370
...that everyone's afraid to approach her?

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.870
I doubt that.

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:09.710
She's kind...

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:11.080
...and really good at helping others.

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:12.330
That's true.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.630
Maybe a lot of guys ask her out.

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:16.380
But she turns them down?

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.710
Turns them down, huh...

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:18.300
Nah.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.880
Maybe she doesn't realize that they're asking her out.

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:22.510
That's possible.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.510
Yuki-chan can be a little clueless...

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.850
...so an indirect approach might not work.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:30.600
Man, the guys in your class are hopeless.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:32.810
Doesn't a single one of them have the guts...

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:35.650
...to confess his passionate feelings to Miyuki?

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:36.940
Guess not...

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:39.610
We don't have enough maniacs in our class.

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:43.910
Miyuki-san's type is usually a bigger hit with maniacs.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:47.010
Maniacs, huh?

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:48.740
Right?

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:49.370
Oh.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:51.580
It's already this late.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:53.720
I'll need to excuse myself.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:55.060
Really?

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:58.850
Please continue to enjoy yourselves.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.960
Then I'll excuse myself.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:02.670
See you later!

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:04.260
Buh-bye.

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:06.930
Anyway...

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.720
Going on with the story...

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:10.310
...that person was actually...

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:12.100
O-Oh?

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:14.390
I-I'm terribly sorry!

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:15.730
Yay!

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:17.560
I-I'm sorry.

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:18.900
Man, oh, man...

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:20.610
Doesn't that always happen?

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:22.860
I did it the other day.

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:24.110
So did I.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.780
Everybody at least does it once.

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:27.990
Right, Konata?

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:28.880
I haven't.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:32.500
That was what you call
an element of turning people on.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:33.790
Miyuki-san.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.000
Good job!

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:42.050
Good lucky!

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:42.880
Okay!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:46.130
Today's another whoo-whoo
happy episode of Lucky Channel!

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.640
I'm your navigator, Akira Kogami.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:49.100
And...

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:49.970
Uh.

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:52.720
I'm Akira-sama's assistant, Minoru Shiraishi.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:53.520
It's a pleasure.

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:54.640
Okay, okay.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:56.730
The two of us have now done this...

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:57.770
Ta-da!

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.650
Three times after today!

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:01.230
How do you feel about it, Shiraishi-san?

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:02.280
Have you gotten used to it?

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:04.320
Not yet...
Well...

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.110
So sorry.

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:10.780
It feels like Shiraishi-san hasn't opened up to me yet.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:13.410
And it looks like we're sitting further apart than usual.

00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:16.290
Is this what they mean by emotional distance?

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:16.750
Sob.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.380
Th-Th-That's not true!

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:19.960
Shuffle.

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:20.750
Okay!

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:23.050
Let's get rollin'!

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:24.090
Um...

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:27.050
We've got something the fans will love today!

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.050
Guess what?

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:31.180
We'll be doing our first
introduction for a member of the regular cast!

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:32.350
Da! Da-da-dum!

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:33.310
Okay, uh...

00:20:33.310 --> 00:20:35.850
We'll be introducing Miyuki Takara-san today.

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.100
Let's see...

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:41.440
The class representative, well-mannered, kn—

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.570
Knowledgeable.

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:46.110
...in both literary and culinary arts. A perfect person.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:46.820
Shiraishi-san.

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:49.200
You know Miyuki-san, right?

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:50.870
But of course!

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:52.620
She's so wonderful, yeah?

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.200
First, there's her glasses!

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:55.910
And then she's pretty as a button.

00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:57.370
With those looks...

00:20:57.370 --> 00:21:00.170
...you'd expect her to be hard to approach...

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:03.000
...but she's actually a friendly person...

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.920
I wish you'd talk that much on the radio show...

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.680
You can't stop talking when it's about Miyuki-san.

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:10.890
No!

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.140
That's not it...

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.220
Well, yeah.

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:15.100
Miyuki Takara-san, is it?

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:16.480
A pretty face.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:17.640
With large breasts.

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:19.390
And various other turn-ons.

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:20.350
Isn't she so lucky to be a pretty character?

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:21.940
Akira-sama, that's a little...

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.570
The maniacs loves her.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:23.820
Uh, maniacs is a little...

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:24.480
But you know...

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:27.610
If it's maniacs you want,
I'm a huge hit with those lolicons...

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:29.280
Too bad!

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:31.030
It's time to say goodbye!

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:32.160
And so...

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:39.040
Send us any questions or
comments about the show please!

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:41.170
Please look forward to next time.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:42.750
See ya!

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:45.500
So what's she really like?

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:47.010
Exactly the same.

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:48.050
No way!

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:51.220
Doesn't she like smoke a pack at a time backstage?

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:53.180
No worry of that. She isn't you.

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.600
That was fun!

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.310
A unique song.

00:22:00.310 --> 00:22:03.480
I'd like to hear a song that
normal people can enjoy already.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:05.980
You know the next one, Kagami.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:08.600
Guess it from the intro!

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.860
It's not another weird song, is it?

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:15.580
What was this song again?

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:16.830
Don't know...

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:17.490
Kagami.

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:18.500
The answer is...

00:22:19.410 --> 00:22:21.080
It's from FMP. FMP.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.130
And it's Kagami's favorite...

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:25.450
Fumoffu!

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:26.340
Really...

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:28.410
I-I just read the novels...

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:29.790
...and got a little hooked.

00:22:33.390 --> 00:22:34.930
You're really good, Kona-chan!

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:37.180
You can also sound like an adult.

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:39.760
Isn't she just doing an imitation?

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:43.650
So?

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:45.650
What are you two going to sing?

00:22:46.310 --> 00:22:48.150
I wonder if there's anything I can sing...

00:22:48.150 --> 00:22:50.280
I don't know very many songs...

00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:51.740
Anything works.

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:52.900
Look at Konata.

00:22:52.950 --> 00:22:55.740
Just sing what you want to!

00:22:55.740 --> 00:22:56.450
Um...

00:22:56.450 --> 00:22:57.990
Then I'll have a look.

00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:00.250
I'm not very confident about my singing...

00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:01.660
It's fine.

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:03.290
We're the only ones who'll hear you.

00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:04.790
Just take it easy.

00:23:04.790 --> 00:23:06.330
Really?

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:07.290
In that case...

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:28.020
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:28.770
I'm Tsukasa.

00:23:28.770 --> 00:23:29.480
Guess what?

00:23:29.480 --> 00:23:33.450
I laughed so hard the other day that I couldn't breathe.

00:23:33.450 --> 00:23:34.320
Then at school one morning...

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:36.040
I'm already out of time?

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:36.660
Next time:

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:37.840
Motivation Issues.

00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:39.990
Look forward to next time!
